# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{research.html}
= Ajay U. Mandlekar -- Research
[https://ee.stanford.edu Department of Electrical Engineering], [https://stanford.edu Stanford University]

== Recent News

- We released our [http://arxiv.org/abs/1911.05321 paper] on offline learning from large-scale robot manipulation datasets and demonstrated that it can learn from our [http://roboturk.stanford.edu/dataset.html crowdsourced RoboTurk dataset] without requiring additional interaction. See our [http://arxiv.org/abs/1911.05321 paper], [https://sites.google.com/stanford.edu/iris/ website], and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H9KZgrI2I7I&feature=emb_title video] for more details! 

- Our recent [https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.04052 paper] is a [https://www.iros2019.org/awards Best Cognitive Robotics Paper Finalist] at IROS 2019! We leveraged [http://roboturk.stanford.edu/ RoboTurk] to create the largest physical robot manipulation dataset ever collected via human teleoperation. See our [https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.04052 paper], [http://ai.stanford.edu/blog/roboturk/ blog post], [http://roboturk.stanford.edu/realrobotdataset website], and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q5uFlJ6hXx8&feature=youtu.be talk]! Dataset coming soon.

- See our [https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.09674 paper], [http://ai.stanford.edu/blog/assistive-latent-spaces/ blog post], and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wjnhrzugBj4&feature=youtu.be video] on learning latent action spaces for assisted teleoperation! 

- Our [https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.04121 paper] on leveraging an ensemble of partial solutions to guide agent exploration during reinforcement learning appeared at CoRL 2019. Check out our [http://ai.stanford.edu/blog/acteach/ blog post], [https://sites.google.com/view/acteach/ website], and [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1QMPpYGrVCo&feature=emb_title talk] for more details!

